; worldtick.eval - EditorTest phase 40 (code-review C78 / C125): one world tick.
;
; The world runs or holds by ONE decision (Game::WorldHeldBy), asked by the one
; tick (Game::TickWorld) whoever owns the input. Read by `worldclock`: the
; world's own count of the updates it took (counted in DungeonWorld::Update),
; so two readings either side of a few frames say whether those frames ran it.
;   pause  - a paused editor stays paused through a bare `editor`, an `editor
;            pick` (the eyedropper) and an `editor issues` - each goes through
;            MapView::SetMode(Editor), the call that used to clear the pause, and
;            the pause is pressed again before each, so each ask fails on its
;            own; `editor off` and back, a real flip, clears it - the control.
;            (`editor tool` is not one: it never asks for the mode, and it
;            saves the picked tool to settings.ini.)
;   frozen - the open console over the paused editor runs nothing; over the
;            running editor it runs (the control).
;   dialog - the open console over an editor dialog runs nothing.
;   sheet  - the character sheet over the level runs the world, the console
;            shut (the control) and open (it used to freeze).
;   exit   - an exit stair stepped onto under the open console is followed: its
;            question goes up, and holds the world.
;   stair  - a stair down stepped onto under the open console is followed: the
;            party arrives on crypt2 with the console still up.
logecho on
reset
timescale 0
freeze on

echo --- pause ---
editor
editor pause on
editor pause
editor
editor pause
editor pause on
editor pick 1 1
editor pause
editor disarm
editor pause on
editor issues
editor pause
editor off
editor pause
editor
editor pause

echo --- frozen ---
; A headless frame is a fraction of a millisecond: at 100x a few of them still
; read as world seconds.
timescale 100
editor pause on
console open
worldclock
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
editor pause off
worldclock
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
console shut

echo --- dialog ---
editor levelsettings open
editor levelsettings
console open
worldclock
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
console shut
presskey esc
editor levelsettings
worldclock

echo --- sheet ---
mappage close
sheet 0
worldclock
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
console open
worldclock
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
console shut
sheet off
timescale 0

echo --- exit ---
goto crypt1
tp 7 7
face s
timescale 100
console open
worldclock
forward 1
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
console shut
timescale 0
presskey esc
worldclock
pos

echo --- stair ---
tp 1 2
face n
timescale 100
console open
worldclock
forward 1
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
pos
worldclock
pos
console shut
timescale 0
echo --- end ---
